{% comment %}
  CartRules — cart page quantity guard (F5 "auto-adjust in cart").
  Add this block anywhere on the cart page template. It inlines the active
  max-quantity rules, plus a key/variant/product map of the cart's lines (the
  rules are keyed by product, but themes mark quantity inputs by line key,
  variant id or line index — never reliably by product id), and
  cartrules-notice.js lowers quantities above a rule's limit and explains why
  in the message box below. The checkout Function stays the real enforcement.
{% endcomment %}

{% assign cache = shop.metafields.cartrules.rules_cache %}
<script type="application/json" id="cartrules-rules-data">
  {% if cache and cache.enabled != false and cache.cartNoticesEnabled != false %}{{ cache | json }}{% else %}{"rules":[]}{% endif %}
</script>
<script type="application/json" id="cartrules-cart-lines">
  [{% for item in cart.items %}{"key":{{ item.key | json }},"variantId":{{ item.variant_id | json }},"productId":{{ item.product_id | json }}}{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}{% endfor %}]
</script>
<script src="{{ 'cartrules-notice.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

<div
  id="cartrules-cart-message"
  class="cartrules-cart-message"
  role="status"
  aria-live="polite"
  style="padding: 0.75rem 1rem; margin: 1rem 0; border-radius: 0.5rem; border: 1px solid rgba(138, 0, 0, 0.35); color: #8a0000;"
  hidden
></div>

{% comment %}
  Renders nothing visible on the live storefront until a quantity is over a
  limit, so in the theme editor merchants would get no visual confirmation
  the block was added at all — surfaced by the App Store review as "widget
  not visible ... in Theme Editor". Show a small placeholder in the editor.
{% endcomment %}
{% if request.design_mode %}
  <div class="cartrules-cart-guard cartrules-cart-guard--placeholder">
    CartRules cart quantity guard — shows a message here and lowers the quantity when a customer goes over a
    maximum-quantity rule.
  </div>
{% endif %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Cart quantity guard",
  "target": "section",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
